  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 846 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nDRIER WEATHER THROUGH THE WEEKEND: \n\nSnow showers are expected in the central mountains until around \nsunrise. Travel in these areas may be impacted by snow and icy \nroads mainly at pass level. Lingering moisture and clearing\nskies could result in pockets of fog into Thursday morning.\nOtherwise conditions become relatively dry. A quick moving \nshortwave skirts the region on Friday which could bring some \nincreased clouds and a few light rain or snow showers over the \nhigher terrain. The moisture is rather limited and the system \nis quick, so expect minor rain and snow amounts for now. A \nbroad ridge of high pressure moves in late this week into the \ncoming weekend, with temperatures warming to above seasonable \nlevels and providing a much needed break from the recent wet \nweather.",
